# GitHub branch protection (rulesets)

`main` must use a **repository ruleset**, not informal discipline only.

## Required ruleset

- **PR required** before merge to `main` (no direct pushes for app code)
- **Status check:** `quality gate` from `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
- **Block force-push** and default-branch deletion

Definition: `.github/rulesets/protect-main.json`  
Apply: `make rulesets-apply` or see `docs/github-rulesets.md`

## Agent behavior

- Never merge or push to `main` for application code.
- Before telling the user a PR is merge-ready, confirm **quality gate** is green on the PR targeting `main`.
- If rulesets are missing (GitHub shows "You haven't created any rulesets"), run or document `scripts/apply-github-rulesets.sh`.

## Private repo note

Rulesets API may return HTTP 403 on GitHub Free private repos — use the manual UI steps in `docs/github-rulesets.md` or upgrade to GitHub Pro.
